WEBVTT

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:05.474
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:06.514 --> 00:00:11.974
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:23.494 --> 00:00:28.764
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:34.134
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:35.374 --> 00:00:40.644
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:46.384
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:46.784 --> 00:00:50.314
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:50.394 --> 00:00:55.324
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.124 --> 00:01:00.464
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.204 --> 00:01:08.164
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.244 --> 00:01:14.144
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tsuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.214 --> 00:01:20.774
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.054 --> 00:01:26.994
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:01:52.884 --> 00:01:53.944
It's nothing.

00:01:58.454 --> 00:02:00.394
I can still do this.

00:02:14.274 --> 00:02:15.464
How is it?

00:02:16.074 --> 00:02:19.704
The data in the PC body itself
is relatively normal.

00:02:19.844 --> 00:02:24.304
But most of the data in
the left arm is black boxed.

00:02:24.454 --> 00:02:26.444
I've never seen anything like it.

00:02:26.754 --> 00:02:28.154
Is it beyond your reach?

00:02:28.384 --> 00:02:30.824
I hope you're not underestimating me.

00:02:31.124 --> 00:02:32.184
I didn't mean to.

00:02:32.554 --> 00:02:35.154
If there's something inside...

00:02:35.224 --> 00:02:37.594
...there's no box that can't be opened.

00:02:41.464 --> 00:02:44.694
So, what do you want to do?

00:02:45.374 --> 00:02:46.334
I don't know.

00:02:47.374 --> 00:02:51.834
I never thought Ovan would disappear.

00:02:52.014 --> 00:02:53.304
You're such a child.

00:02:53.784 --> 00:02:54.744
Why?

00:02:55.084 --> 00:02:58.314
Yesterday is like today is like tomorrow.

00:02:58.384 --> 00:03:00.814
Did you think it would last forever?

00:03:00.884 --> 00:03:02.374
It's not like that.

00:03:03.124 --> 00:03:06.754
Ovan might never come back.

00:03:07.494 --> 00:03:09.294
Why do you think that?

00:03:09.494 --> 00:03:10.924
It's only a game.

00:03:10.994 --> 00:03:13.464
And there are a million online games.

00:03:13.804 --> 00:03:16.134
With things the way they are...

00:03:16.204 --> 00:03:18.434
...it's not likely he'll come back.

00:03:18.504 --> 00:03:20.664
But isn't Shino waiting?

00:03:23.204 --> 00:03:27.204
That's because she believes in Ovan.

00:03:27.314 --> 00:03:29.444
And how about you?

00:03:29.644 --> 00:03:32.204
You don't believe in Ovan?

00:03:32.284 --> 00:03:34.984
Whether I believe or not...

00:03:35.054 --> 00:03:37.584
...I hardly know who Ovan is.

00:03:38.224 --> 00:03:41.094
I wonder if there's any reason
for me to be here.

00:03:41.394 --> 00:03:42.554
What do you mean?

00:03:42.994 --> 00:03:45.554
Well, Ovan isn't here anymore.

00:03:46.094 --> 00:03:49.594
So, you were playing this game
for that eccentric man?

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:50.704
No.

00:03:51.004 --> 00:03:54.904
Then, why don't you play for the ones
still in the game?

00:04:01.314 --> 00:04:02.834
Teacher, why don't you sit down?

00:04:04.184 --> 00:04:06.514
We didn't know anything, did we?

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:08.044
What do you mean?

00:04:08.124 --> 00:04:09.524
About Ovan.

00:04:10.224 --> 00:04:12.284
Only that he's a mysterious man.

00:04:12.494 --> 00:04:15.554
If you didn't know anything,
how would I?

00:04:15.624 --> 00:04:16.524
You know...

00:04:16.594 --> 00:04:17.224
Huh?

00:04:17.294 --> 00:04:18.734
What do you think about this place?

00:04:18.794 --> 00:04:21.284
You mean our @home?

00:04:21.664 --> 00:04:24.264
No, stupid. I mean the Twilight Brigade.

00:04:24.504 --> 00:04:26.804
Don't you think there's no reason for it now?

00:04:27.104 --> 00:04:28.074
No reason?

00:04:28.374 --> 00:04:32.274
It was a guild created in order to find
the Key of the Twilight.

00:04:32.644 --> 00:04:34.474
Didn't Shino tell you?

00:04:35.614 --> 00:04:38.744
She said rather than emailing each
other every time we logged on...

00:04:38.814 --> 00:04:41.614
...it would be easier to play
if we were in the same guild.

00:04:42.454 --> 00:04:46.724
I figured if Shino was around
I could have fun with the game!

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:51.494
I'm quitting.

00:04:51.564 --> 00:04:52.534
Why?

00:04:52.794 --> 00:04:56.964
Shino has Haseo,
and Ovan won't be back.

00:04:57.504 --> 00:04:59.564
And if the Key of the Twilight doesn't exist...

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:02.504
...there's no rationale for this guild.

00:05:02.574 --> 00:05:04.334
But maybe it does exist.

00:05:04.414 --> 00:05:07.144
Even Shino said it doesn't exist.

00:05:07.484 --> 00:05:09.414
Yeah but, it's a game.

00:05:09.614 --> 00:05:13.274
There's always an objective to a game.

00:05:13.754 --> 00:05:16.084
But the Key of the Twilight is different.

00:05:17.354 --> 00:05:18.824
You really think so?

00:05:18.954 --> 00:05:21.424
Rather than having hope and
losing hope repeatedly...

00:05:21.494 --> 00:05:24.934
...don't you think it's better to do
something different and have fun?

00:05:26.494 --> 00:05:29.404
It's pointless to force
yourself to play a game.

00:05:29.464 --> 00:05:31.064
I'm not forcing myself!

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:32.934
That attitude...

00:05:33.004 --> 00:05:34.134
It's the same as before.

00:05:35.474 --> 00:05:36.994
You are forcing yourself, aren't you?

00:05:37.574 --> 00:05:39.404
Oh, stop it!

00:05:51.254 --> 00:05:52.484
Well, I'm off.

00:05:52.554 --> 00:05:53.784
Come any time.

00:05:54.024 --> 00:05:56.994
I'm not planning on
quitting any time soon.

00:05:57.094 --> 00:05:57.854
Yeah.

00:05:57.964 --> 00:05:59.024
I'll see you later.

00:06:00.904 --> 00:06:03.024
Are you here for life advice, too?

00:06:04.034 --> 00:06:05.404
Killing time.

00:06:08.844 --> 00:06:11.404
How's the Brigade been lately?

00:06:11.674 --> 00:06:12.644
Same old.

00:06:13.144 --> 00:06:15.804
So Ovan hasn't come back yet.

00:06:18.014 --> 00:06:23.384
Shino can be very fragile when
her weak points are pushed.

00:06:24.654 --> 00:06:26.094
Be a support to her.

00:06:26.154 --> 00:06:27.524
You're telling me that, too?

00:06:56.524 --> 00:06:57.514
Ovan...

00:07:05.564 --> 00:07:06.554
Haseo.

00:07:14.874 --> 00:07:17.034
Bset was worried about you.

00:07:18.314 --> 00:07:19.174
I see.

00:07:21.344 --> 00:07:22.314
You know.

00:07:22.844 --> 00:07:23.474
Hm?

00:07:24.254 --> 00:07:25.344
Well...

00:07:25.484 --> 00:07:27.114
You don't seem well.

00:07:27.554 --> 00:07:29.384
Why don't you log out for today?

00:07:29.784 --> 00:07:33.224
Logging out won't bring Ovan back.

00:07:33.564 --> 00:07:35.964
This isn't the time to run away.

00:07:36.624 --> 00:07:38.794
Run away from what?

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:40.594
I wonder.

00:07:44.504 --> 00:07:47.474
Shino, you must be tired.

00:07:47.604 --> 00:07:49.094
Are you sleeping well?

00:07:49.374 --> 00:07:50.434
I guess.

00:07:51.244 --> 00:07:52.934
You know...

00:07:53.074 --> 00:07:56.204
...if you need someone to talk to...

00:07:58.954 --> 00:08:00.314
But I don't know...

00:08:07.524 --> 00:08:11.294
I feel like I need to support the brigade.

00:08:12.064 --> 00:08:14.654
But with Sakisaka
acting the way he is...

00:08:14.734 --> 00:08:17.134
...I think it's getting
to be too much for me.

00:08:17.204 --> 00:08:21.264
I think you should ignore
what Sakisaka says.

00:08:22.104 --> 00:08:22.834
But...

00:08:23.374 --> 00:08:25.034
I'll take care of things.

00:08:31.114 --> 00:08:32.174
Thank you...

00:08:33.754 --> 00:08:34.724
...Haseo.

00:08:43.734 --> 00:08:47.964
Ovan seemed like he was
bound to do something great.

00:08:48.234 --> 00:08:52.064
Well, he did have that
kind of charisma about him.

00:08:52.134 --> 00:08:52.934
Right?

00:08:53.004 --> 00:08:56.404
I think that's why I expected so much.

00:08:57.514 --> 00:08:59.804
You know, I came to realize...

00:08:59.874 --> 00:09:00.704
Huh?

00:09:00.914 --> 00:09:02.474
...what my feelings were.

00:09:03.084 --> 00:09:07.384
I stayed in the game
because Ovan was here.

00:09:11.924 --> 00:09:14.654
Ovan's not coming back, is he?

00:09:14.924 --> 00:09:16.794
Why are you asking me?

00:09:17.094 --> 00:09:18.394
You know, don't you?

00:09:20.504 --> 00:09:22.264
Besides, Gord quit.

00:09:24.104 --> 00:09:26.034
I think I'm going to quit too.

00:09:26.204 --> 00:09:27.634
I won't stop you.

00:09:27.974 --> 00:09:29.164
You sure are cold.

00:09:29.874 --> 00:09:33.204
If that's what you decided, I can't stop you.

00:09:33.374 --> 00:09:34.814
I guess so, but...

00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:37.904
At least one more time...

00:09:40.454 --> 00:09:42.354
...I wanted to see Ovan.

00:09:44.494 --> 00:09:45.324
Yo!

00:09:47.164 --> 00:09:49.064
Sorry, I'm late.

00:09:49.164 --> 00:09:50.654
So, what's this about?

00:09:50.734 --> 00:09:54.894
I think we should start searching for
the Key of the Twilight again.

00:09:55.234 --> 00:09:55.994
What?

00:09:56.064 --> 00:09:57.554
Are you serious?

00:09:57.634 --> 00:10:00.624
Haven't you been listening
this entire time?

00:10:01.004 --> 00:10:03.494
There is no Key of the Twilight.

00:10:03.714 --> 00:10:05.644
It's not about whether or not it exists.

00:10:05.714 --> 00:10:07.734
Don't you remember what Ovan used to say?

00:10:07.814 --> 00:10:10.144
I'm not stupid enough
to go looking...

00:10:10.214 --> 00:10:12.114
...for something that doesn't exist.

00:10:12.184 --> 00:10:14.114
I don't care if it's stupid.

00:10:14.184 --> 00:10:16.154
What do you think, Shino?

00:10:16.524 --> 00:10:17.544
What do you mean?

00:10:17.624 --> 00:10:19.954
You think we should start
looking for it again?

00:10:22.694 --> 00:10:25.824
There's no reason to look for something
that doesn't exist.

00:10:30.404 --> 00:10:31.894
Three against one.

00:10:32.174 --> 00:10:35.234
I'd rather not waste my time like before.

00:10:35.304 --> 00:10:36.244
Before?

00:10:36.344 --> 00:10:38.574
You probably don't know about it.

00:10:38.674 --> 00:10:41.114
But when there was no information...

00:10:41.314 --> 00:10:47.254
...we spent hours searching every field
based on groundless rumors.

00:10:47.324 --> 00:10:49.984
We guarded the Lost Grounds
all day long, for days.

00:10:50.054 --> 00:10:51.084
For real?

00:10:51.494 --> 00:10:53.284
A waste of time, don't you think?

00:10:53.454 --> 00:10:54.324
Yeah.

00:10:55.324 --> 00:10:58.454
If you want to search for it,
bring some tangible information.

00:11:00.164 --> 00:11:00.894
Don't do it.

00:11:03.304 --> 00:11:06.164
Anyway, why don't we try looking for Ovan?

00:11:06.274 --> 00:11:08.174
It seems like he's still logged in...

00:11:08.244 --> 00:11:10.404
...so he's got to be somewhere.

00:11:10.614 --> 00:11:11.834
Even if he's still here...

00:11:11.914 --> 00:11:15.174
...we can't get in contact
and he hasn't come back.

00:11:15.244 --> 00:11:17.514
Looking for him is pointless.

00:11:17.614 --> 00:11:20.414
Why don't you try before
you say it's pointless?

00:11:23.424 --> 00:11:25.654
How do we look for him?

00:11:25.854 --> 00:11:27.084
I don't know.

00:11:27.164 --> 00:11:28.854
I don't know about this.

00:11:29.124 --> 00:11:32.464
Yeah, but we can't just keep sitting here.

00:11:32.534 --> 00:11:35.394
Haven't we done enough?
It's time to stop hoping.

00:11:35.464 --> 00:11:37.194
Aren't you worried?

00:11:37.374 --> 00:11:39.364
Ovan's not a kid.

00:11:39.504 --> 00:11:41.974
If he wants to come back, he will.

00:11:42.074 --> 00:11:45.104
He's ignored our communications
because he doesn't want to.

00:11:45.174 --> 00:11:47.544
Worrying about him is a waste of time.

00:11:49.314 --> 00:11:50.974
You're an idiot, Teacher!

00:12:02.364 --> 00:12:04.884
Why did you do that all of a sudden?

00:12:05.034 --> 00:12:08.764
I thought if we had a goal
it would unite us again.

00:12:11.274 --> 00:12:12.604
I guess I messed up.

00:12:19.544 --> 00:12:20.514
You know what?

00:12:21.584 --> 00:12:23.344
I'm going out for a bit.

00:12:41.464 --> 00:12:43.364
S-Stop.

00:12:44.074 --> 00:12:45.054
Stop it.

00:12:52.744 --> 00:12:54.044
Just a little more.

00:13:04.824 --> 00:13:07.054
S-Stop!

00:13:09.524 --> 00:13:10.554
Stop it!

00:13:13.764 --> 00:13:16.534
I didn't think I'd ever come back.

00:13:17.904 --> 00:13:18.894
Welcome back.

00:13:19.734 --> 00:13:20.464
No.

00:13:21.474 --> 00:13:22.994
I'm thinking of quitting.

00:13:23.574 --> 00:13:25.664
So I wanted to say good-bye.

00:13:25.744 --> 00:13:26.714
I see.

00:13:27.284 --> 00:13:29.714
I wanted to ask you something.

00:13:29.884 --> 00:13:30.874
What?

00:13:31.354 --> 00:13:33.814
What do you think of Haseo?

00:13:35.254 --> 00:13:37.274
He's a good kid, isn't he?

00:13:37.954 --> 00:13:38.824
Yes.

00:13:41.894 --> 00:13:44.484
Why don't you depend on him...

00:13:44.564 --> 00:13:46.724
...and forget about Ovan.

00:13:46.894 --> 00:13:48.164
I can't do that.

00:13:50.934 --> 00:13:54.064
Ovan is very special to me.

00:13:56.474 --> 00:13:59.064
I'll never be able to top you.

00:13:59.974 --> 00:14:01.034
I'm sorry.

00:14:02.744 --> 00:14:06.444
No, you helped me make up my mind.

00:14:08.854 --> 00:14:10.254
Well, I'm going.

00:14:10.454 --> 00:14:11.354
Okay.

00:14:38.854 --> 00:14:41.374
I worked so hard to keep myself together.

00:14:46.154 --> 00:14:47.144
Shino...

00:14:48.024 --> 00:14:48.994
What...

00:14:50.794 --> 00:14:52.384
...should I do?

00:15:05.174 --> 00:15:06.334
What...

00:15:08.214 --> 00:15:09.874
...should I do?

00:15:11.854 --> 00:15:14.684
Everyone's going to leave, aren't they?

00:15:15.084 --> 00:15:18.074
You shouldn't be so sad about it.

00:15:18.224 --> 00:15:21.094
It's not that I'm sad.

00:15:22.294 --> 00:15:23.814
I wonder...

00:15:24.394 --> 00:15:27.234
...maybe I'm different from everyone.

00:15:27.834 --> 00:15:29.064
Different?

00:15:29.504 --> 00:15:34.664
I think I'll stay in this world until it's gone.

00:15:36.544 --> 00:15:38.704
No matter what kind of world it becomes.

00:15:39.574 --> 00:15:41.014
Because of Ovan?

00:15:43.844 --> 00:15:46.374
Maybe I shouldn't have introduced you to him.

00:15:46.984 --> 00:15:48.784
I'm grateful to you.

00:15:50.184 --> 00:15:53.754
But I just need some time.

00:15:53.824 --> 00:15:54.794
Time?

00:15:55.064 --> 00:15:57.424
To come to terms with my feelings.

00:15:59.294 --> 00:16:00.494
I understand.

00:16:01.734 --> 00:16:03.634
If it has to be broken up...

00:16:08.504 --> 00:16:10.604
...I want to be the one who does it.

00:16:14.544 --> 00:16:16.204
Huh? Where's Shino?

00:16:16.544 --> 00:16:19.104
Phyllo contacted me...

00:16:19.184 --> 00:16:21.484
...and said Shino won't be
logging in for a while.

00:16:26.294 --> 00:16:28.764
My email bounced back again.

00:16:31.994 --> 00:16:34.154
Why, at a time like this?

00:16:35.034 --> 00:16:37.004
I was an idiot to believe it!

00:16:37.164 --> 00:16:38.324
What is this about?

00:16:39.174 --> 00:16:42.294
Ovan was working with TaN...

00:16:42.374 --> 00:16:44.934
...and they have the Key of the Twilight!

00:16:45.314 --> 00:16:46.274
What?

00:16:46.844 --> 00:16:50.044
Just think about it calmly.
It makes perfect sense.

00:16:50.614 --> 00:16:52.104
That's why Shino...

00:16:52.184 --> 00:16:53.874
What are you saying?

00:16:54.384 --> 00:16:57.114
She said the Key of the Twilight doesn't exist.

00:16:57.184 --> 00:16:59.054
Then why hasn't he come back?!

00:16:59.154 --> 00:17:00.854
He's been logged in the whole time!

00:17:00.964 --> 00:17:03.294
There has to be an explanation for it.

00:17:03.364 --> 00:17:06.264
Like what? Shino doesn't know.

00:17:06.434 --> 00:17:08.794
Why wouldn't he be able to return?

00:17:09.504 --> 00:17:10.464
Well...

00:17:11.804 --> 00:17:13.134
What?

00:17:25.284 --> 00:17:27.444
I can't do this anymore.

00:17:29.724 --> 00:17:31.154
I'm leaving.

00:17:31.224 --> 00:17:32.124
Teacher!

00:17:39.434 --> 00:17:40.724
You're not going after him?

00:17:43.004 --> 00:17:44.234
But...

00:17:57.514 --> 00:17:59.884
Stop it...

00:18:04.554 --> 00:18:06.284
Stop it!

00:18:18.434 --> 00:18:20.304
Did you get a message from Shino?

00:18:20.404 --> 00:18:21.104
No.

00:18:23.274 --> 00:18:25.264
I thought someone called me.

00:18:25.374 --> 00:18:26.964
It was probably your parents.

00:18:27.044 --> 00:18:29.134
No. I live by myself.

00:18:29.484 --> 00:18:31.444
Hey, Haseo?

00:18:32.684 --> 00:18:35.344
Do you know Shino's phone number?

00:18:35.754 --> 00:18:36.724
No.

00:18:37.754 --> 00:18:39.154
I haven't asked her yet.

00:18:39.494 --> 00:18:40.454
Not yet?

00:18:42.324 --> 00:18:45.024
I think if I ask she'd give it to me.

00:18:47.034 --> 00:18:49.894
If I'd known this would happen,
I should have asked.

00:18:52.504 --> 00:18:54.404
You two have been getting
along well lately.

00:18:55.074 --> 00:18:56.474
Not really.

00:18:56.674 --> 00:18:58.644
But you're always together.

00:18:58.774 --> 00:18:59.974
No, we're not.

00:19:00.044 --> 00:19:03.484
But you're always staring at Shino.

00:19:03.744 --> 00:19:05.444
What are you trying to say?

00:19:05.514 --> 00:19:07.544
It's not fair.

00:19:07.754 --> 00:19:10.444
Well, you're always with Sakisaka.

00:19:11.624 --> 00:19:13.284
It's not because I want to.

00:19:14.694 --> 00:19:15.884
What do you mean?

00:19:16.364 --> 00:19:19.994
You wouldn't understand the way I feel.

00:19:20.164 --> 00:19:21.634
I don't want to know.

00:19:21.704 --> 00:19:25.324
You'd be satisfied if I'm with Teacher, right?

00:19:28.674 --> 00:19:30.664
I never said that.

00:19:49.064 --> 00:19:50.114
What's going on?

00:19:50.624 --> 00:19:53.184
I'm leaving the Brigade too.

00:19:55.234 --> 00:19:56.364
Are you sure?

00:19:56.434 --> 00:19:58.734
I have more fun with you anyway!

00:19:59.204 --> 00:20:00.174
I see.

00:20:00.734 --> 00:20:01.724
Sorry about that.

00:20:01.944 --> 00:20:03.874
That's not like you.

00:20:04.444 --> 00:20:07.904
Hey, let's practice our Rengeki attack
like we used to.

00:20:08.144 --> 00:20:11.634
I don't really feel like it, but why not.

00:20:12.854 --> 00:20:16.444
I'm perplexed that we both
ended up leaving...

00:20:16.524 --> 00:20:19.544
...and I'm surprised that
we're still together!

00:20:20.124 --> 00:20:22.714
I haven't heard it in a while,
a Sakisaka-ism!

00:20:23.594 --> 00:20:24.964
Well, you know.

00:20:48.354 --> 00:20:50.324
I read your email.

00:20:51.194 --> 00:20:52.084
Right.

00:20:52.694 --> 00:20:56.594
I'm sorry I left you alone
at such a difficult time.

00:20:56.824 --> 00:20:58.794
It doesn't matter. I'm fine.

00:20:58.864 --> 00:21:00.454
I made a decision.

00:21:00.534 --> 00:21:01.194
Huh?

00:21:14.814 --> 00:21:19.184
I won't be like Aura
who lost hope and ran away.

00:21:19.554 --> 00:21:21.914
What happened to you?

00:21:22.354 --> 00:21:23.214
This?

00:21:23.284 --> 00:21:25.684
I guess it's a way of expressing my resolve.

00:21:32.134 --> 00:21:35.624
Today, I'm going to disband
the Twilight Brigade.

00:21:36.404 --> 00:21:37.924
Is that okay?

00:21:38.634 --> 00:21:40.224
Even if there is no guild...

00:21:40.904 --> 00:21:42.934
Even if I'm the only one...

00:21:43.704 --> 00:21:47.164
I can wait until Ovan comes back.

00:21:54.554 --> 00:21:56.244
You won't be the only one.

00:21:57.684 --> 00:21:58.844
I...

00:21:59.624 --> 00:22:00.814
...will wait with you.

00:22:02.694 --> 00:22:03.714
Thank you.

00:22:04.264 --> 00:22:05.094
You don't...

00:22:05.164 --> 00:22:07.634
...need to thank you, right?

00:22:07.904 --> 00:22:10.264
As long as you understand.

00:22:29.554 --> 00:22:33.154
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.224 --> 00:22:36.664
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:36.924 --> 00:22:40.334
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:40.394 --> 00:22:44.764
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:48.274 --> 00:22:51.804
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:51.874 --> 00:22:55.574
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:55.644 --> 00:23:02.884
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:02.954 --> 00:23:06.614
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:06.694 --> 00:23:10.384
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:10.464 --> 00:23:17.394
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:17.564 --> 00:23:21.304
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:21.374 --> 00:23:24.394
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:24.474 --> 00:23:31.934
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.184 --> 00:23:35.674
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:35.784 --> 00:23:39.484
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:39.594 --> 00:23:43.184
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.264 --> 00:23:46.824
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:46.894 --> 00:23:50.634
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:50.704 --> 00:23:54.394
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:55.474 --> 00:23:56.664
Next Episode
